    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Smithville became the county seat of modern‑day Lawrence County in 1837 before the seat moved in 1869.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smithville%2C_Arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Smithville's relocation of the county seat in 1869 was partly to tap riverboat commerce along the Black River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
